 "circuits": [],
 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Topology",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Four diodes form a full-wave bridge. Each ~ lead joins the cathode of a diode from - and the anode of a diode to +; the anodes of two diodes meet at -, the cathodes of the other two at +. An AC voltage across the two ~ leads appears rectified between + and -."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Current derating",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The full 2.0 A average output holds up to a lead temperature of 100 °C, then falls in a straight line to zero at about 150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Surge",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "A single 8.3 ms half-sine surge may reach 60 A. Repeated cycles lower the allowed peak: about 29 A at 10 cycles and about 16 A at 100 cycles."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction and soldering",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The body is moulded plastic; the compound is rated UL 94V-0, RoHS-compliant and halogen-free. The leads are solder plated and solderable to MIL-STD-750, Method 2026. Soldering at 260 °C for 10 seconds with 5 lb (2.3 kg) of tension on the leads is guaranteed."
  }
 ],
